     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Those need a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and all three require stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc (needs admin_dc) and dump_dbadmin_adfs (needs admin_adfs). admin_dc needs foothold_dc, which only auth_dc gives, and auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin. admin_adfs needs foothold_adfs, which only auth_adfs gives, and auth_adfs also requires NOT mfa_admin. The deployed mfa:admin defence makes mfa_admin true, so both are blocked, even though the attacker can still get reach_internal and stolen_admin via kerberoasting. As a result stolen_dbadmin can never become true, and exfiltrated is unreachable.\"}"
    }
   ],
